==Problem 25==
An airplane has <imath>4</imath> rows of seats with <imath>3</imath> seats in each row. Eight passengers have boarded the plane and are distributed randomly among the seats. A married couple is next to board. What is the probability there will be <imath>2</imath> adjacent seats in the same row for the couple?

<asy>
// Asymptote by aoum
import roundedpath;
unitsize(1cm);

path p = roundedpath((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle, 0.1);

for (int r = 0; r < 4; ++r) {
  for (int c = 0; c < 3; ++c) {
    draw(shift(1.1 * c, 1.3 * r) * p);
  }
}
</asy>

<imath>\textbf{(A)}\ \dfrac{8}{15} \qquad \textbf{(B)}\ \dfrac{32}{55} \qquad \textbf{(C)}\ \dfrac{20}{33} \qquad \textbf{(D)}\ \dfrac{34}{55} \qquad \textbf{(E)}\ \dfrac{8}{11}</imath>

